      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127924,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 344,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127925,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 344,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AEH has a predilection for the forearms and the lateral aspect of the neck.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127926,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 344,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion manifests as an asymptomatic, small papule or plaque developing in sun-exposed skin {12196746; 31268926}. Multiple lesions are exceptional {35170476}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127927,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 344,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AEH is rare. It occurs in middle-aged and elderly adults, with a slight female predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127928,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 344,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It is likely that chronic sun damage plays a role in the development of lesions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127929,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 344,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127930,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 344,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127931,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 344,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AEH shows a band-like proliferation of capillaries, each surrounded by a layer of pericytes and oriented parallel to the epidermis in the upper reticular dermis. There is background solar elastosis.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>Microvenular haemangioma involves the mid to deep dermis and is poorly defined and not associated with solar elastosis. Poikilodermatous plaque-like haemangioma is also a superficial plaque-like proliferation but the lesions are larger, the stroma is oedematous, elastic fibres are missing, and there is no solar elastosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
